From: Tom Tromey <tom@tromey.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gdb/dwarf: don't assert when a unit's "pretend" language changes

Backport of the dwarf2_per_cu::set_lang hunk from upstream commit
329a53a6d590e2e90f590c89473990040a86c8e0 ("Some cleanups to 'pretend
language' handling"), which is not in any gdb release as of 17.2.

    Bug: https://sourceware.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=33661

A compilation unit that has no DW_AT_language of its own inherits the
"pretend" language of whichever unit referenced it first
(follow_die_offset passes source_cu->lang ()).  Because
dw2_instantiate_symtab drops every cached dwarf2_cu via
free_cached_comp_units, such a unit is re-read on each symtab
expansion, and a later referrer can supply a different language.  The
old code asserted that this never happens:

  dwarf2/read.c:19295: internal-error: set_lang: Assertion
  `old_value == language_unknown || old_value == language_minimal
   || old_value == lang' failed.

This reproduces with ELFs that link TI ARM Codegen objects, which emit
cross-unit DW_FORM_ref4 references into a small shared unit carrying
the base types and no DW_AT_language.

Replace the assertions with compare-exchanges, so the first settled
language wins and later "pretend" languages are ignored.

diff --git a/gdb/dwarf2/read.c b/gdb/dwarf2/read.c
index d43a6e1f343..a3a4df3345d 100644
--- a/gdb/dwarf2/read.c
+++ b/gdb/dwarf2/read.c
@@ -19288,17 +19288,23 @@ dwarf2_per_cu::set_lang (enum language lang, dwarf_source_language dw_lang)
   if (unit_type () == DW_UT_partial)
     return;
 
-  /* Set if not set already.  */
+  /* A unit without DW_AT_language takes the "pretend" language of
+     whichever unit happened to reference it first, so the same unit can
+     legitimately be prepared more than once with different languages.
+     In practice that is fine, because DIEs shared across languages are
+     limited to constructs those languages agree on.  Once a language has
+     been settled on, keep it.  */
+  packed<language, LANGUAGE_BYTES> expected1 = language_unknown;
+  packed<language, LANGUAGE_BYTES> expected2 = language_minimal;
   packed<language, LANGUAGE_BYTES> new_value = lang;
-  packed<language, LANGUAGE_BYTES> old_value = m_lang.exchange (new_value);
-  /* If already set, verify that it's the same value.  */
-  gdb_assert (old_value == language_unknown
-	      || old_value == language_minimal
-	      || old_value == lang);
 
+  if (!m_lang.compare_exchange_strong (expected1, new_value))
+    m_lang.compare_exchange_strong (expected2, new_value);
+
+  /* Likewise for the DWARF language, which has a single unknown value.  */
+  packed<dwarf_source_language, 2> old_dw = (dwarf_source_language) 0;
   packed<dwarf_source_language, 2> new_dw = dw_lang;
-  packed<dwarf_source_language, 2> old_dw = m_dw_lang.exchange (new_dw);
-  gdb_assert (old_dw == 0 || old_dw == dw_lang);
+  m_dw_lang.compare_exchange_strong (old_dw, new_dw);
 }
 
 /* See read.h.  */
